From b81717891cf3f38390bf1eeab2e8d31f59c56e48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:58:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] agents: confirm the person is still active before
 background work acts as them

Scheduled conversations, resumed waits, decision follow-ups, queued messages
and a portal task's wait started turns as the conversation's owner without
checking that the owner was still a member of the organization with an active,
unlocked account. A deactivated or locked user's schedules kept asking the
agent in their name. Evaluation replay checked status but not the lock.

personaccess.Check is the one rule (the same read and test that end a
signed-in session). Every background path that acts as a person calls it
before acting and, on a refusal, skips with the reason: the schedule's Skipped
result, the evaluation's skip message, a logged skip for waits and follow-ups,
and a held reason for a queued message. A resumed wait also checks the owner
may still use the conversation's agent before starting the turn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
