+Work that runs as a person after the request that asked for it has ended (a scheduled
+conversation, a wait picked up, a decision follow-up, a queued message, an evaluation
+replay, a portal task's wait) asks `personaccess.Check` first: the person must still be a
+member of the organization with an active, unlocked account, the same test that ends a
+signed-in session. A refusal skips the work with its reason (the schedule's `Skipped`, the
+evaluation's skip message, a log line) and nothing runs as them; the work then checks the
+access it needs (`MayUseAgent` on the conversation's agent) as before.
+
